univ_2:sics_univ_2_18: EXCLUDED_CASES.tsv BOUNDED_MAX_ARITY_ONLY: condition(\+ current_prolog_flag(max_arity,unbounded)) -- builds a list of max_arity+1 elements before {_ =.. [f|L]} expecting error(representation_error(max_arity)); at 1024 that was 1025 elements and the case passed, at 2147483647 (SCRIP 4f612be5d) it is 2^31 elements and the case dies in the trail arena in m3 and m4 (the cfo, univ_2 33/33 -> 32/33 against a built control); a cured trail raises resource_error, which this case does not accept, so it measures a small-max_arity system, not SCRIP (CEO-1540; the hard-cap row is prolog-exhausting-the-heap-cap-or-the-trail-arena-ends-the-run-where-swipl-raises-a-catchable-resource-error)
write_term_3:lgt_write_term_3_132: EXCLUDED_CASES.tsv NO_ORACLE_ANSWER: asserts '[1,2,3|...]' for write_term([1,2,3,4,5],[max_depth(3)]), GNU Prolog's text; the pinned oracle swipl 9.0.4 prints '[1,2|...]' and the marker-less program is the default dialect, which takes SWI (CEO-1536) -- the fifth evidence form, cto CEO-2117
write_term_3:lgt_write_term_3_134: EXCLUDED_CASES.tsv NO_ORACLE_ANSWER: asserts '[1|...]' for write_term([1,2,3,4,5],[max_depth(1)]), GNU Prolog's text; the pinned oracle swipl 9.0.4 prints '[...|...]' and the marker-less program is the default dialect, which takes SWI (CEO-1536) -- the fifth evidence form, cto CEO-2117
